Backport vLLM PR #51034: SSE keep-alive comments for idle streaming responses.

When a long request is queued or in prefill, vLLM streams no bytes for many
seconds, and the reverse proxy / tunnel in front (Bifrost here, minimum idle
of 120s unless configured, and its idle timer counts real body bytes only --
TCP keepalive probes do not reset it) closes the connection, dropping the
answer. This backports the upstream `with_sse_keep_alive` wrapper plus the
--sse-keep-alive-interval CLI flag, which emit an SSE comment line (": keep-
alive") whenever a streaming /v1/chat/completions or /v1/completions response
is idle for the configured number of seconds. SSE-compliant clients ignore
the comments; proxies still count the bytes.

Upstream: commit 585bb07c7 (PR #51034) applied to vLLM 0.28.0. The three
original hunks landed unchanged; paths are relative to the vllm package
(patch -p1 -d <site-packages>/vllm). Deviations from upstream:
  - tests dropped (this repo patches the installed package, no test tree)
  - single-user frontend args, so the flag is --sse-keep-alive-interval
    (set in start_qwen.sh)

